# Pipeline outputs — regenerated every run, never committed.
#
# Anchored to the repository root. An unanchored `report.md` matches at every
# depth, which silently swallowed `eval/report.md` — a file the README, the wiki
# and CONTRIBUTING all describe as committed so that a regression shows up as a
# diff. Nothing failed; the deliverable simply was not there, and `npm run eval
# --gate` would have failed on a fresh checkout looking for a file git had been
# told to hide.
/results.json
/analysis.json
/report.md
/otel-spans.json
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Run history lives in the CI cache (ADR-0004), not in git.
.flakemetry/history.json

# Local SQLite data for the demo app.
app/server/*.db
app/server/*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.eslintcache
/eval/report-all.md
/eval/metrics-all.json

# TaskFlow's development database. State, not source — the seed script rebuilds it.
.taskflow/
